        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Efflorescence is salt left behind by water that came through your wall. Brush it off dry, clean the rest with vinegar or a buffered masonry cleaner, and save the muriatic acid for the rare case that needs it. Never coat over it.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Then go outside. Gutters, downspouts, grading and window wells fix most of it. What comes back after that is a drainage problem, and no amount of paint on the inside of the block will make it a paint problem.
          </p>
        </div>

